2. Technical SEO & Performance
Page Speed & CWV: We recommend running PageSpeed Insights and Lighthouse for both pages. Given our pages rely on JavaScript (content hidden from crawl), they may have higher TTFB or slow LCP. Action: Optimize by deferring non-critical scripts, compressing images (use modern formats), and enabling browser caching/CDN. Ensure largest contentful paint (calculator form) loads quickly. (Axis Bank’s SPA was heavy but loaded content promptly; Paytm’s page was very long, so their speed is unknown but likely slower – we must aim for fast performance.)

Mobile Usability: All competitor sites are mobile-responsive. Ensure BharatSaver’s calculators have mobile-friendly design (responsive input fields/buttons). Test on Google Mobile-Friendly Test and fix any layout issues. Using a responsive framework or CSS tweaks may be needed for our form.

Core Web Vitals: Monitor LCP (Largest Contentful Paint) – likely the calculator form or banner image. Optimize by inline-critical CSS, lazy-loading offscreen images. Minimize CLS (avoid layout shifts from form loading). Ensure FID (First Input Delay) is low: our calculators should respond instantly (debounce input handlers if heavy).

Indexability & Canonical: Verify our /en/apy-calculator and /en/jeevan-utsav-calculator are in XML sitemap and not blocked by robots.txt. Use canonical tags if duplicate versions exist. (Axis Bank page has canonical SEO, likely BharatSaver too). If content is injected by JS, ensure server-side rendering or prerendering so Google can index text.

Structured Data: Add JSON‑LD markup. In particular, implement FAQPage schema using our FAQ Q&As. This can win rich snippets. (Example code given below.) For Jeevan Utsav, also consider HowTo or QAPage for the step-by-step guide. Ensure valid schema by testing with Google’s Rich Results tool. No competitor seems to use JSON-LD, so adding this is a quick win.

